<!--
    kuna: the two-register value a rustc Result/Option is returned in survives
    (see kuna-rustabi.xml) but has no NAME and no SHAPE. It renders as a raw
    16-byte container, the tag and the payload are byte offsets into it, and
    which variant a return site builds is nowhere in the output.

    Stage / sub-stage: P5 types, aggregate-union.
    P0 assertion:      option rustadt off|auto|always  (default off).

    Source (rustc, -C opt-level=2, x86-64, bytes verbatim below; #[inline(never)]):

        pub fn branchy(x: u32, y: u32) -> Result&lt;u32, u32&gt; {
            if x &lt; 11 { return Ok(x.wrapping_add(y).wrapping_mul(3)); }
            if y &gt; 100 { return Ok(y - 1); }
            Err(x ^ y)
        }

        branchy: mov %esi,%edx ; cmp $0xb,%edi ; jae L1 ; add %edi,%edx
                 lea (%rdx,%rdx,2),%edx ; xor %eax,%eax ; ret
             L1: cmp $0x64,%edx ; jbe L2 ; dec %edx ; xor %eax,%eax ; ret
             L2: xor %edi,%edx ; mov $0x1,%eax ; ret

    Three RETURNs, the tag a literal 0 on two of them and 1 on the third: the
    two-variant tagged case.

    The bug (pass 1, the default): the return type is `undefined16`, the two Ok
    paths render as a shift that buries the payload in the top half
    (`ZEXT416(...) &lt;&lt; 0x40`), and the Err path writes byte offsets into an
    anonymous char array. Nothing says there are two variants, which one a path
    builds, or where the payload lives.

    The fix (pass 2, option rustadt always): a struct of a tag plus a union of
    two payload structs is synthesized and installed as the recovered return
    type, each return site's union facet is pinned from the guard that fixed its
    tag (never from ScoreUnionFields, which cannot see control flow and ties on
    two same-width members), and a site whose value is one expression renders as
    the variant constructor. `always` rather than `auto` because a bytechunk
    carries no `.comment` record for the source-language detection to read.

    The NEGATIVE half (samevariant, hand-assembled, verbatim below):

        samevariant: mov %esi,%edx ; cmp $0xb,%edi ; jae L ; add %edi,%edx
                     xor %eax,%eax ; ret
                  L: dec %edx ; xor %eax,%eax ; ret

    The same two-register return shape with the same discriminant-shaped low
    half, but ONE tag value across both paths. One tag is not two variants, so
    the pass refuses and the function must render IDENTICALLY in both passes.
-->
